  "behavior": [
    "Every hard-cut shot is an ordinal-aligned native sequence layer with explicit identity transform. All plate children are in a single full-timeline native required-coverage group; viewport alpha threshold remains 254/255 on every root frame and shutter sample.",
    "Native pinned-font labels and separate qualification/caption layers; authored dark panels; projected anchor leaders hide honestly for occluded/behind/clipped/hidden targets. Explicit offscreen indicators cannot count as visible target reading proof.",
    "Explicit font axes need actual pinned fvar ranges supplied by preflight; ranges propagate to font asset.variable and authored instance axes to native text styles. Missing prepared ranges fail located.",
    "Caption cue timings and complete narration metadata are preserved. Supplied PCM sample counts are used directly; no fabricated narration padding.",
    "Native measured text bounds are required to establish layout acceptance. Missing bounds stay estimated. Checks cover every sidecar frame, overlap, offscreen, protected region, truthful anchor visibility, and consecutive30-frame holds.",
    "Semantic CE12 reading declarations enforce simultaneous exact value/unit/qualification text with measured fully visible bounds, opacity/reveal, stable glyph pose, low speed, and no member overlap. Cuts reset intervals. Unannotated defaults remain unchanged.",
    "Purposeful static reading can classify existing raw frozen codes as warnings only if the measured complete readable interval covers the raw run and all painted state is stationary. Raw code/range/measurement/severity are retained. Frozen pixels over changing media or moving paint remain errors.",
    "Native video/sequence paint signature includes actual selected asset/source identity/frame pair rather than advancing sourceSeconds. Hold-frame and independent rendered pixel freeze errors remain intact.",
    "Only proven line mask y extents changed: raster layout ascent/descent replaced by per-line ascent/descent for mixed-size runs. Thai shaping/count-fit were not changed."
  ],
